From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 02:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Include unistd.h after the prelude on macOS, for MonolithPy

MonolithPy's Python.h includes mp_embed.h, which renames read, close,
pread, pwrite, lseek, access and faccessat with macros before the system
headers declare them, then defines its own inline versions. On macOS,
MainProgram.c included <unistd.h> ahead of the prelude for the app
bundle's getcwd and chdir, so the system declarations came first and every
compile against MonolithPy stopped with:

    mp_embed.h: error: static declaration of 'close' follows non-static
    declaration

The prelude includes <unistd.h> through Python.h anyway; the explicit
include now follows it.
---
 nuitka/build/static_src/MainProgram.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nuitka/build/static_src/MainProgram.c b/nuitka/build/static_src/MainProgram.c
--- a/nuitka/build/static_src/MainProgram.c
+++ b/nuitka/build/static_src/MainProgram.c
@@ -16,11 +16,13 @@
 #include <windows.h>
 #endif
 
+#include "nuitka/prelude.h"
+
+// After the prelude: MonolithPy's mp_embed.h, which Python.h includes, has
+// to come before the system headers to rename what it replaces.
 #if defined(__APPLE__)
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
-
-#include "nuitka/prelude.h"
 
 #if _NUITKA_ONEFILE_MODE && !defined(_WIN32)
 #include <errno.h>
-- 
